course: dictionary
lesson: 14668
title: Planned in advance
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Premeditated means planned or thought about carefully beforehand. The start, pre-, means before, and meditated means thought over, so the word tells you the plan was made earlier, not on the spur of the moment. «The thief's escape was premeditated: he had drawn a map of the building a week earlier.» The map shows the plan came first.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Words like planned, a week earlier or practised tell you that something was premeditated. «She shouted in a sudden burst of anger» is the opposite: nothing was planned beforehand. Ask yourself: was this decided before, or did it just happen?
explain: Law and crime stories use this word often, because courts usually treat a premeditated crime as more serious than one done in a sudden moment. In ethics lessons, it helps you compare harm done on purpose with harm done by accident. «The vase broke by accident, but the window was smashed on purpose, after a careful plan.»
fact: Premeditated is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a premeditated crime.
fact: Pre- means before, so premeditated means thought about before it happens.
fact: «Premeditated» means planned or thought about carefully beforehand, especially a crime or a bad act.
fact: «A premeditated crime» is planned, not done in a sudden moment.
fact: Courts usually treat premeditated crimes as more serious than crimes done on the spur of the moment.
exercise: «The robbery was premeditated: the gang had practised the plan for months.» What does premeditated mean? | Done by accident | *Planned well in advance | Loud and messy | Finished very quickly
exercise: Which word means the opposite of premeditated? | Careful | Secret | *Accidental | Planned
exercise: «The vase broke by accident, but the window was smashed on purpose, after a careful plan.» Which harm was done on purpose? | The broken vase | Both were accidents | Neither was harmful | *The broken window
test: A ___ crime is planned long before it happens. | happy | *premeditated | careless | sudden
test: Which clue shows that a plan was premeditated? | He ran away fast | The thief was tall | *He drew a map of the bank a week before | It was raining that night
exam: Why do courts often treat a premeditated crime as more serious? | Because nobody saw it happen | Because it was done in the dark | *Because it was planned, not done in a sudden moment | Because it was done by a child
